# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored; this file is not, so keep it empty.
#
# Every wa-agent command reads ./.env from the directory you run it in (only there:
# not a parent directory, not your home directory). It only fills gaps: a variable
# your shell already exports always wins. When .env supplied or duplicated one of the
# variables below, the command says so on stderr, by name and never by value:
#
#     env: WHATSAPP_AGENT_TOKEN from ./.env; GEMINI_API_KEY from the shell (./.env also sets it, not used)
#
# `wa-agent --no-env-file <command>` skips this file entirely. The library never
# reads it: a program that imports wa_agent sees only its own environment. Format:
# KEY=VALUE lines, # comments, an optional `export `, and '…' or "…" taken literally.


# The WhatsApp Agent Platform token: the only variable `send` and `recv` need.
# Get it in the WhatsApp app: Settings > Agents > your agent > Chat info > API key.
# An agent may only message its own creator, so this token can reach nobody but you.
# Alternative if you would rather it not sit in your environment: keep it in a file
# and pass `--token-file ~/.wa-token`. Order: a token exported in the shell, then
# --token-file, then this file.
WHATSAPP_AGENT_TOKEN=

# Transcription keys, read by `wa-agent transcribe` and `recv --transcribe`.
# Optional: without one, voice notes still arrive, marked `transcribed: false`, and
# `recv` warns once rather than refusing to run. Which variable is read follows
# `--provider` (gemini unless you say otherwise), never whichever happens to be
# set; point `--key-env NAME` elsewhere if you keep a key under a different name.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# `--provider local` (offline Whisper, `pip install "wa-agent[local]"`) needs no key. The models it
# uses are downloaded by `wa-agent model pull` into $XDG_DATA_HOME/wa-agent/models, or
# ~/.local/share/wa-agent/models: data, so not under the state directory below. Never your
# working directory. Nothing downloads during `recv`.
# XDG_DATA_HOME=

# Where the poll cursor, the message log and downloaded media live. Optional;
# defaults to ~/.local/state/wa-agent/<profile>. Never your working directory.
# Use `--profile NAME` to keep two agents apart rather than pointing this at each.
# XDG_STATE_HOME=

# Set to 1 to print a traceback when something fails. Off by default: a failure
# prints one line naming its code (`error [platform_rejected]: …`) and nothing else.
# See docs/errors.md for every code and whether retrying helps.
# WHATSAPP_AGENT_DEBUG=
